{
  "id": "Compound::DB01016 - Gene::3767",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Glyburide and Kcnj11 through a shared pathway involving sulfonylurea compounds. Glyburide, as a sulfonylurea, is included in the class of antidiabetic agents, which in turn includes Tolazamide and Glimepiride. All three compounds bind to Kcnj11, indicating a common mechanism of action. The lowest common ancestor of Glyburide and Tolazamide points to N-Sulfonylurea, reinforcing the classification of these compounds as antidiabetic agents. The evidence suggests that Glyburide may act through a shared pathway with Tolazamide, which binds to Kcnj11, thereby supporting a potential role for Glyburide in modulating Kcnj11 activity. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of sulfonylurea compounds in interacting with Kcnj11, suggesting a broader pharmacological relationship that may be elucidated further.",
